{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490357-v20-help-for-a-one-shot-session","id":1490357,"title":"[V20] Help for a one-shot session","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-16T01:16:21-07:00","id":1490357,"title":"[V20] Help for a one-shot session","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I have to lead a session in a bar for players who are both new and experienced in role-playing games and Vampire, the Masquerade. Vampire is a saga game par excellence for me, allowing long developments. So I'm very annoyed because I have a hard time seeing what to do for such a diverse audience in just 3 or 4 hours. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> Thank You !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8969-grands-pas","name":"Grands-Pas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T07:04:57-07:00","id":1490385,"title":"","content":"Start by checking the basics, describe the situation &amp; enviroment.<br /> <br /> - Who are the players' characters, clans, backstories, allies/contacts/relations/etc?<br /> - Are those characters already familiar with each other?<br /> - Where does the story start so to speak (it's kind of dubious in your post if the story in a bar or <b><i>you are going to ST for a group of people</i></b> in a bar, could you clear that up)?<br /> <br /> Just give people in the forum some more details, so we can get a better idea of what is the matter and try to give some specific and useful answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-16-2022, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T07:22:55-07:00","id":1490389,"title":"","content":"I am, as a storyteller, going to run a game for a group of mostly unknown people, in a public place (a bar), some being familiar with role playing and vampire the masquerade and others absolutely new to both. I had in mind to provide the characters, the sheets being already filled, and the starting situation \u2013 whatever it may be. The difficulty lies in coming up with an interesting storyline that would fit into a single 3 or 4 hour session, because I would probably never see these people again. It's an initiation. So the story has to be over by the end of the evening. And I don't have many ideas for something that short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8969,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8969-grands-pas","user":"Grands-Pas","date":". 08-16-2022, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8969-grands-pas","name":"Grands-Pas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T12:07:13-07:00","id":1490419,"title":"","content":"I think you have several challenges.<br /> <br /> You want to be sure the players have a chance to use their powers. You want to make sure it is clear to them that their characters are vampires, not superheroes though. And you want to evoke the kind of story and tropes people associate with vampires.<br /> <br /> I recommend ignoring most vampire politics, the Prince's court, etc. That'll just eat up too much time. You want to keep things minimal in regards to the domain around them. If they get messed up in that, it'll eat all the time you have yet give the PCs little to do. Keep NPCs at a minimum.<br /> <br /> You don't want a railroad. Whatever you do, make sure the players can determine their own approaches and solutions. That is what keeps the game fun.<br /> <br /> You need an antagonist that can be defeated in 3-4 hours, and that can provide a challenge to the PCs. It might be a mortal hunter, another vampire, a Lupine, or somebody else well equipped deal with the vampire PCs.<br /> <br /> I suggest opening up the game with all characters fairly new to the city. They've been introduced to the Prince and are legal to stay. They know his name, but don't know anything else about the domain. They've been told there are areas where it is open for all vampires of the domain to feed. The PCs all meet each other at some night club - or other locale you think works - where vampires are allowed to feed. This may not be their first time at this club, but it is the first time all the PCs have been in the club at the same time. Have there be someone at the club who is Masquerade safe, likely a ghoul, who looks out for trouble. He can then tell each PC since he knows they are new here that they may find it useful to meet another of their kind (the other PCs already at the club). There should not be any other vampires at this club. But you can use this ghoul NPC to handle anything the players may need or their questions.<br /> <br /> Then have the players introduce themselves to each other. What do they tell the other PCs? They should describe their character's physical appearance and mannerism. They should give some kind of explanation as to why they've just travelled to this city/domain (this is something that you as the ST might want to help them with. Maybe create some index cards with a brief backstory that can be randomly shuffled and handed out. That way the player doesn't need to come up with something on the fly. Have more index cards/backgrounds than you need, just in case a player doesn't like the one he pulled and give him a redraw. The backgrounds here are not meant to be plot fodder, just something realistic and evocative/interesting that gives an idea of the setting). It's up to them how much they want to reveal, or even if they want to lie to the others. It's just meant to allow for some roleplay between the PCs and allow each player to explore their character concept. And make it clear each PC knows no one else in this city. Other than the Prince, this is the extent of their knowledge of other vampires.<br /> <br /> Then have them roll randomly for their initial Blood Pool count. Then let each run a brief hunting/feeding scene IF that PC is interested in doing so. Who do they select as their target? What do they do as their hunting style? Do any cooperate together in the hunt? Let them roleplay it out in a relative place of safety. But if they screw up - that is OK. Make it part of the story.<br /> <br /> That should eat up a good hour or so. Then you hit them with an event that they must deal with - the antagonist does something. Maybe it happens inside the club. Maybe it happens outside the club. Maybe the ghoul gets a phone call, and he involves the PCs. But make sure there is some immediate motivation for the PCs. Either their lives are directly threatened, or they'll get blamed for something bad if they don't act, or it is an opportunity for them to earn a boon from a powerful vampire, or gain favor of the Prince, or whatever. Just make sure if the PCs refuse to become involved, there is an immediate consequence to it. And that consequence then becomes the story.<br /> <br /> Then let them come up with the solution. Maybe it is to kill the antagonist. Or win the antagonist over as an ally. Or deal with it in an indirect manner. Let them decide what to do. They may do the thing many new players want to do - drop the problem off to an NPC, perhaps the Prince. If so, be ready with a response so the Prince drops the problem back on them (by threat, coercion, favor, or whatever else works for you).<br /> <br /> Then have one or two complications ready, if you know you need to kill more time before the session is up. If you are running out of time, don't use complications. Just let them enact their plan.<br /> <br /> Players tend to eat up a lot of time discussing their plans and next steps, so you may not need to do too much. You need to keep it simple.<br /> <br /> This is how I would proceed. You just need to figure out the details (the antagonist, what he wants, and what he does that affects the PCs).<br /> <br /> <br /> Some ideas on generic backgrounds you could hand out:<ul><li>The vampire is on the run (could be an Anarch, just someone an elder didn't like, someone who was framed or set-up or in the wrong place at wrong time, Blood Hunted, etc.)</li> <li>Sire sent her to a new city to expand his powerbase</li> <li>Choose to come here to escape the confines/control of their sire or clan</li> <li>Explored the limits of their previous domain, and moving to a new city for more opportunities or excitement</li> <li>Mortal members of their old family have left here, and they want to continue to oversee them</li> <li>She was abandoned by her sire and came here as the nearest city to find other vampires to help her navigate new existence</li> <li>Sire was attacked by people called &quot;the Sabbat&quot; and destroyed. She fled here for safety.</li> <li>Wanted to start over in new city as she was caught up in the intrigues of her sire and his enemies in the old one, and wanted nothing to do with it</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T12:41:34-07:00","id":1490422,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8969-grands-pas","name":"Grands-Pas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T13:35:02-07:00","id":1490434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grands-Pas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490357-v20-help-for-a-one-shot-session?p=1490389#post1490389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am, as a storyteller, going to run a game for a group of mostly unknown people, in a public place (a bar), some being familiar with role playing and vampire the masquerade and others absolutely new to both. I had in mind to provide the characters, the sheets being already filled, and the starting situation \u2013 whatever it may be. The difficulty lies in coming up with an interesting storyline that would fit into a single 3 or 4 hour session, because I would probably never see these people again. It's an initiation. So the story has to be over by the end of the evening. And I don't have many ideas for something that short.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Black Fox has given good advice, however I find some of those things a little to nuanced to what the game is if you're just gonna play for a few hours, some of them have never played and you'll never see them again.<br /> So, keep it simple. Very simple.<br /> <br /> DO give them pre-made chars. Ask them what kind of person they would like to portray and give them a related pregen (party guy/girl: Toreador. College quarterback? Brujah)<br /> Forget about backgrounds, princes, domains and all that. At the beginning of the session, have them already be vamps mass-embraced at a party.<br /> <br /> DO railroad. Again you're just gonna play for a few hours. What I think is that you should come with a story based on movies (like the example above: they all got turned into vampires at a party) You need to give them a specific problem for them to solve in the 3 or so hours you're going to play. As per the idea that I'm working in this post, they all awake at the party they where at, all their friends are dead and they have a hazy memory of some strangers killing everyone (<i>Where they</i><i> biting them?!)</i> Take them through the realization that they are now vampires: Lusting for the blood splattered all over the walls, getting burned by the sun, etc. Now they are going to try and find whoever did this to them. Leave some clues to get them started.<br /> <br /> It's a simple idea that can be followed through in a few hours. Is it vastly original? No, but cliches exist for a reason. Are they going to experience all the intricacies of VTM? No, but again, time. Hopefully they'll have fun, and maybe they'll play the game again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","user":"HeavyWhiskey","date":". 08-16-2022, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T17:48:09-07:00","id":1490463,"title":"","content":"What I'd add is, chose one element of the game, a theme with associated mechanic, to showcase. This can be the Frenzy, Humanity and Degeneration, the valor of Willpower, Clan Disciplines, Blood Pool and Feeding, whatever.<br /> <br /> This will be the centerpiece of your short story (do NOT use more than one, that'll only dilute the effect). Think a scene or a few ways to make this theme come up. You don't even need to actually use the mechanic, as long as it is a possibility you can use the scene to show what could have happened.<br /> <br /> You'll be able to come up with characters, situations, scenes and put things together easier with a unifying theme in mind, and will drive home one of the key aspects of the game (do <b>not</b> worry at showcasing everything, just your centerpiece and whatever comes naturally).<br /> <br /> Unless you need something else to run your theme, I actually think it better to given them a set starting Blood Pool. Something between 4 and 6 will work better, as it is enough for them to function while still making the decision to hunt a valid one, so it is on the table without the risk to hijack your game. If you want a survival race against the sun as they reach a new city and must feed, starting at 1 or 2 is a good idea, if you want a showdown of vampiric power without basic needs getting in the way they can start at max or near it.<br /> <br /> Railroad depends too much on you, but while I tend to agree more with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> here you do need to have a limited scope for the story and ways to bring the PCs to the plot if they get lost. As a rule of thumb, they should always have an obvious option on where to go to have the plot going forward. If you don't want to railroad, you also have to be able to embrace new paths and just use whatever the players try to accomplish as the new goal. Did they decide to bring matters to the Prince? If they're really keen on it, maybe just making the search for the Prince in time be their goal. Do they want to ignore the plot and pursue something else? Accept that something else and/or hit them with whatever consequence for ignoring the plot and run with that, not as a punishment, but just as the story happening.<br /> <br /> I have some experience with this kind of play. I ST'd in events many times, with mixed groups of strangers. The hard part at the beginning is keeping things to a minimum, because it is easier to stretch them during play than shortening them. The other is to not drop the ball, you don't need to intervene while the players are engaged discussing in-character and having fun, but whenever they stop truly clueless on what to do you should drop a clue and/or some action to keep the pace.<br /> <br /> Other than that, the old saying of not worrying and having fun. It's not a big deal if the session doesn't come to a proper end. If time is up just wrap things with whatever you have, either jump to the main scene using whatever happened until then as a guide to set it or make it into a short narration with references to what happened in play and call it a day. Your players know as much as you that time is short and they're likely to forgive you such hiccups as long as you're honest with them about this. If they end up really wanting to see the rest of the game you couldn't deliver, that's not a failure, but a success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T00:03:16-07:00","id":1490490,"title":"","content":"I have read all your advice and want to thank you all. It got me back on track to focus on a short and effective session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8969-grands-pas","name":"Grands-Pas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}